2026-10-09T18:53:48.3904993Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-09T18:53:48.3916400Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4019975Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4030469Z [0m
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4031236Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4031794Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4032038Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4032864Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4033773Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4034556Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4035044Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4035778Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4036118Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4036857Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4037512Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4038380Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4038747Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4038907Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4039139Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4039385Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4039648Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4040014Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4040140Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4040267Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4040419Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4040798Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4041299Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4044418Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4044598Z I will:
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4044792Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4045128Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4045648Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4046471Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4047137Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4047427Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4048036Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4048798Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4049488Z    /root
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4061927Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4062922Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4074568Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4075828Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4076613Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4077328Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4078318Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4096463Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4097303Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4108200Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4109085Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4109899Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4110259Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4110583Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4110989Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4111484Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4112302Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4112705Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4112878Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4113174Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4113347Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4113561Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4113909Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4114047Z 
2026-10-09T18:53:48.4114061Z 
